# Instructions short of arguments or given invalid ones. Observed: a
# fixed-arity instruction short of arguments pops what the stack holds and
# runs with zeros; a looped instruction short of them is skipped; CINDEX
# outside the stack pushes zero, MINDEX does nothing; a zone other than 0 or 1
# is ignored; a negative loop count ends the program; a point outside its zone
# leaves the instruction without effect.
# Each glyph's program computes values and writes value i into the y of
# point i of a 32-point contour (SCFS along y), so the dump shows them.
heights 16384
fpgm
  PUSH 0; FDEF; ENDF
end
glyph advance 400
  contour 0 0, 10 0, 20 0, 30 0, 40 0, 50 0, 60 0, 70 0, 80 0, 90 0, 100 0, 110 0, 120 0, 130 0, 140 0, 150 0, 160 0, 170 0, 180 0, 190 0, 200 0, 210 0, 220 0, 230 0, 240 0, 250 0, 260 0, 270 0, 280 0, 290 0, 300 0, 310 0
  contour 0 0, 300 100, 100 700, -200 50, 1000 999, 3 7, 1500 -1300, 77 1
  contour 0 0, 10 0, 20 0, 30 0, 40 0, 50 0, 60 0, 70 500
  program
    PUSH 0; PUSH 5; ADD; SVTCA[0]; SCFS
    PUSH 1; PUSH 77; SVTCA[0]; SCFS
  end
end
